"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>, [Fe(H<sub>2</sub>O)<sub>4</sub>)OH)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>+</sup>, [Fe(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>(CN)<sub>4</sub>]<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sup>, [Co(NH<sub>2</sub>-CH<sub>2</sub>-CH<sub>2</sub>-NH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>2</sub>(NH<sub>3</sub>)Cl]<sup>2+</sup> and [Co(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>4</sub>(H<sub>2</sub>O)Cl]<sup>2+</sup>, the number of complex ions that shows cis-trans isomerism is ______________.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"6","explanation":"<p>The complex is with MA<sub>2</sub>B<sub>4</sub> or MA<sub>4</sub>B<sub>2</sub> or M(AA)<sub>2</sub>B<sub>2</sub> or M(AA)<sub>2</sub>BC structure can exhibit cis-trans isomerism. Therefore, number of given complex ions showing cis-trans isomerism is 6.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"isomerism-in-coordination-compounds","type":"integer","year":2015,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2015-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l0w0alz8","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2015-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pthree-moles-of-bsub2subhsub6sub-are-completely-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-mpsdputaabk0edd8","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>Three moles of B<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub> are completely reacted with methanol. The number of moles of boron containing product formed is ____________.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"answer":"6","explanation":"<p>The reaction is</p>\n<p>B<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub> + 6CH<sub>3</sub>OH <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 2B(OCH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub> + 6H<sub>2</sub></p>\n<p>From the reaction, 1 mol of B<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub> reacts with 6 mol of CH<sub>3</sub>OH to produce 2 mol of B(OCH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>.</p>\n<p>Therefore, 3 mol of B<sub>2</sub>H<sub>6</sub> would react with 18 mol of CH<sub>3</sub>OH to produce 6 mol of B(OCH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"group-13-elements-boron-family","type":"integer","year":2015,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"jee-advanced-2015-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l0w0d2ll","chapter":"hydrocarbons","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":2,"paperId":"jee-advanced-2015-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pin-the-following-reactions-the-product-s-isp-pimage-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chem